# Pairs with MovedStreamKeepsAckedWrites, and needs two moves (the TwoMoves
# variant's instance; the mutation declares the second move itself). The flip
# requires A durable fence to be held rather than THIS move's
# (WalMoveFenceCore.IsFlipAdmitted compares move ids). Move m1 copies; its lease
# lapses and the source releases the fence and serves an append; move m2 raises
# its own fence; m1's flip then sees a fence held and cuts over to its copy,
# which lacks the append. The base flip requires the fence to name this move.
MODULE: MovedStreamKeepsAckedWritesFlipAcceptsAnyMovesFence
TARGET: MovedStreamKeepsAckedWrites
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the flip accepts another move's fence, so a move whose own fence was released still cuts over and drops a write
PERTURBS: MoveSwitch

--- FIND
    /\ move[m] = "copied"
    /\ dfence = m
    /\ durable' = {o \in moveCopy[m] : o >= tail}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: any move's fence admits the flip.
    /\ move[m] = "copied"
    /\ dfence # NoMove
    /\ durable' = {o \in moveCopy[m] : o >= tail}
--- END

--- FIND
MoveIds == {"m1"}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the defect needs a second move.
MoveIds == {"m1", "m2"}
--- END